# Normalize text files to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true -- the default
# on GitHub's windows runners, and on most local Git for Windows installs
# -- rewrites every text file to CRLF on disk. Prettier is configured with
# `endOfLine: "lf"`, so it then flags the entire tree. That is exactly how
# CI failed while `npm run format:ts:check` passed locally: the checked-out
# bytes differed from the committed ones, so the two were never running the
# same check.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than plain `text=auto`) is what makes the working tree
# match the repository, which is the property prettier and rustfmt actually
# depend on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch. `text=auto` detects most of these on its
# own, but the sidecar executables and model weights are large and being
# explicit costs nothing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.bin binary
*.param binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
